<title>LEBANON: Beirut weekly T-bill issue raises 535.9 bln pounds.</title>
<headline>Beirut weekly T-bill issue raises 535.9 bln pounds.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lebanon's weekly treasury bill issue of January 30 raised 535.9 billion Lebanese pounds, the finance ministry said on Monday.</p>
<p>The previous issue raised 467.9 billion pounds.</p>
<p>The new issue posted a nominal surplus of subscription against maturity of 198.8 billion pounds. It raised the following amounts (in billions of pounds, previous week in brackets):</p>
<p>    Term			  Yield		    Amount</p>
<p>    Three months	    14.08 (14.17)	  55.2    (34)</p>
<p>    Six months		15.56 (15.89)	  135.5  (133)</p>
<p>    12 months		 15.84 (16.38)	  145.1 (92.9)</p>
<p>    24 months		 17.14 (18.12)	  200.1  (208)</p>
<p>The Lebanese pound closed at $1,549.75 to the U.S. dollar on Monday from 1,550.25 a week earlier and 1,591 a year ago.</p>
<p>-Beirut editorial (961 1) 602057 745307 745308</p>
